# SeKretSauce

macOS Security Suite - Finding and closing macOS security gaps.

*"Blind guy makes software for Blind Spots" -RyCat*

## Phase 1: Core Security Tools (In Progress)

### Rampart - Unified Firewall Control
**Status: Built**

"One Place to Rule Them All" - GUI + CLI for managing:
- pf (packet filter) - BSD-level network filtering
- Application Firewall - Per-app network control
- Network monitoring - Live connections and listeners

Location: `rampart/`

```bash
cd rampart && ./build.sh
```

## Phase 2: Security Scanners (Planned)

- [ ] Secret scanner - Find bad secrets in files
- [ ] Password file detector - Find password-protected files
- [ ] Crypto wallet finder - Detect cryptocurrency wallets
- [ ] CA auditor - Audit installed certificate authorities
- [ ] Unsigned binary detector - Find unsigned macOS files
- [ ] Signed binary auditor - Audit signed macOS files
- [ ] Browser extension scanner - Check for malicious extensions
- [ ] Chrome/Google store search

## Phase 2: Brewster (Planned)

Homebrew security auditor:
- Find malicious packages
- Flag suspicious items
- Package signature verification

Location: `brewster/`

## Phase 3: MalMonitor (Future)

Behavioral malware detection:
- Process monitoring
- File system access patterns
- Network behavior analysis
- Persistence detection
- TCC bypass detection

## Architecture

```
SeKretSauce/
├── rampart/          # Phase 1 - Unified Firewall (DONE)
│   ├── FirewallKit/     - Core library
│   ├── FirewallHelper/  - Privileged XPC helper
│   ├── CLI/             - Command-line interface
│   └── GUI/             - SwiftUI application
│
├── brewster/         # Phase 2 - Homebrew auditor
├── pkg/              # Phase 2 - Go scanner modules
│   ├── secrets/
│   ├── wallet/
│   ├── ca/
│   ├── certs/
│   ├── browser/
│   ├── keychain/
│   └── breach/
│
└── Sources/          # Phase 3 - Swift components
    ├── EndpointSecurity/
    ├── NetworkExtension/
    └── TunnelDetection/
```

## Requirements

- macOS 13.0+
- Swift 5.9+
- Go 1.21+ (for scanners)
- Developer ID (for code signing)

## Quick Start

```bash
# Build Rampart (Phase 1)
cd rampart && ./build.sh

# Install CLI
sudo cp build/rampart /usr/local/bin/

# Check firewall status
rampart status
```
